-- coa19-a1-records.l4: Part 25, Chapter A1, cross-heading "Companies' records and registers": ss 859P and 859Q, lines 11815-11841
-- of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law as the text states it.
--
-- SEAMS taken as inputs (PLAN.md section 4), MAYBE BOOLEAN so that "not covered" in the answering section stays "not covered" here:
--   `s 1105 Documents that may be drawn up and delivered in other languages` (coa24): s 859P(5).
--   `s 1136 Regulations about where certain company records to be kept available for inspection` (coa25): s 859Q(2)(b).
--   `s 1121 the officer is in default` (coa24) and `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` (keel): s 859Q(5)(b).
-- "such fee as may be prescribed" (s 859Q(4)(b)) is a plain NUMBER input: the amount is set outside the Act.

§ `Part 25 Company charges -- Chapter A1 -- Companies' records and registers (ss 859P and 859Q)`

§§ `s 859P Companies to keep copies of instruments creating and amending charges`

-- src:11817 | (1) A company must keep available for inspection a copy of every—
-- src:11818 | (a) instrument creating a charge capable of registration under this Chapter, and
-- src:11819 | (b) instrument effecting any variation or amendment of such a charge.
@ref s 859P(1) A company must keep available for inspection a copy of every instrument creating a charge or effecting a variation or amendment (src:11817-11819)
GIVEN `the instrument creates a charge capable of registration under Chapter A1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument effects a variation or amendment of such a charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859P(1) the company must keep a copy of the instrument available for inspection` MEANS
    IF `the instrument creates a charge capable of registration under Chapter A1` OR `the instrument effects a variation or amendment of such a charge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "A company must keep available for inspection a copy of every—": the list names two kinds of instrument and is not closed with "only"

-- src:11820 | (2) In the case of a charge contained in a series of uniform debentures, a copy of one of the debentures of the series is sufficient for the purposes of subsection (1)(a).
@ref s 859P(2) In the case of a charge contained in a series of uniform debentures, a copy of one of the debentures of the series is sufficient (src:11820-11820)
GIVEN `the charge is contained in a series of uniform debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company keeps a copy of one of the debentures of the series` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859P(2) a copy of one of the debentures is sufficient for subsection (1)(a)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the charge is contained in a series of uniform debentures`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a charge contained in a series of uniform debentures"
        IF `the company keeps a copy of one of the debentures of the series` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what is sufficient, not what is insufficient

-- src:11821 | (3) If the particulars referred to in section 859D(1) or the particulars of the property or undertaking charged are not contained in the instrument creating the charge, but are instead contained in other documents which are referred to in or otherwise incorporated into the instrument, then the company must also keep available for inspection a copy of those other documents.
@ref s 859P(3) the company must also keep available for inspection a copy of those other documents (src:11821-11821)
GIVEN `the particulars referred to in section 859D(1) or the particulars of the property or undertaking charged are not contained in the instrument creating the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are instead contained in other documents which are referred to in or otherwise incorporated into the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859P(3) the company must also keep a copy of those other documents available for inspection` MEANS
    IF `the particulars referred to in section 859D(1) or the particulars of the property or undertaking charged are not contained in the instrument creating the charge` AND `they are instead contained in other documents which are referred to in or otherwise incorporated into the instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the particulars referred to in section 859D(1) or the particulars of the property or undertaking charged are not contained in the instrument creating the charge, but are instead contained in other documents which are referred to in or otherwise incorporated into the instrument, then the company must also keep"

-- src:11822 | (4) It is sufficient for the purposes of subsection (1)(a) if the company keeps a copy of the instrument in the form delivered to the registrar under section 859A(3), 859B(3) or (4) or 859C(3).
@ref s 859P(4) It is sufficient for the purposes of subsection (1)(a) if the company keeps a copy of the instrument in the form delivered to the registrar (src:11822-11822)
GIVEN `the company keeps a copy of the instrument in the form delivered to the registrar under section 859A(3), 859B(3) or (4) or 859C(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859P(4) keeping a copy in the form delivered to the registrar is sufficient for subsection (1)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the company keeps a copy of the instrument in the form delivered to the registrar under section 859A(3), 859B(3) or (4) or 859C(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what is sufficient, not what is insufficient

-- src:11823 | (5) Where a translation has been delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 1105, the company must keep available for inspection a copy of the translation.
@ref s 859P(5) Where a translation has been delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 1105, the company must keep available for inspection a copy of the translation (src:11823-11823)
GIVEN `s 1105 Documents that may be drawn up and delivered in other languages` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859P(5) the company must keep a copy of the translation available for inspection` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1105 Documents that may be drawn up and delivered in other languages`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a translation has been delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 1105"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a translation was delivered in accordance with s 1105 is another section's answer

§§ `s 859Q Instruments creating charges to be available for inspection`

-- src:11825 | (1) This section applies to documents required to be kept available for inspection under section 859P (copies of instruments creating and amending charges).
@ref s 859Q(1) This section applies to documents required to be kept available for inspection under section 859P (src:11825-11825)
GIVEN `the documents are required to be kept available for inspection under section 859P` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859Q(1) this section applies to the documents` MEANS
    IF `the documents are required to be kept available for inspection under section 859P`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to documents required to be kept available for inspection under section 859P": a scope statement with no "only" (as in s 860(7), fork F-C2)

-- src:11826 | (2) The documents must be kept available for inspection—
-- src:11827 | (a) at the company's registered office, or
-- src:11828 | (b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136.
@ref s 859Q(2) The documents must be kept available for inspection at the company's registered office or at a place specified in regulations under section 1136 (src:11826-11828)
GIVEN `the documents are kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1136 Regulations about where certain company records to be kept available for inspection` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859Q(2) the documents are kept at a place the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `the documents are kept at the company's registered office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1136 Regulations about where certain company records to be kept available for inspection`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The documents must be kept available for inspection—": a bare "must", not met (fork F-P1 in NOTES.md)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the places specified in regulations under s 1136 are another section's answer

-- src:11829 | (3) The company must give notice to the registrar—
-- src:11830 | (a) of the place at which the documents are kept available for inspection, and
-- src:11831 | (b) of any change in that place,
-- src:11832 | unless they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office.
@ref s 859Q(3) The company must give notice to the registrar of the place and of any change in that place, unless they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office (src:11829-11832)
GIVEN `the documents have at all times been kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859Q(3) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place and of any change in that place` MEANS
    IF `the documents have at all times been kept at the company's registered office`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (3) in time: the text gives no period for the notice; the offence in (5) arises when "default is made for 14 days". The status of the notice is therefore
-- counted in days of default: see (5).

DECLARE `s 859Q(4) terms of inspection` IS ONE OF
    `s 859Q(4)(a) open to inspection without charge`
    `s 859Q(4)(b) open to inspection on payment of the prescribed fee` HAS `the fee in pounds that is prescribed` IS A NUMBER

-- src:11833 | (4) The documents must be open to the inspection—
-- src:11834 | (a) of any creditor or member of the company, without charge, and
-- src:11835 | (b) of any other person, on payment of such fee as may be prescribed.
@ref s 859Q(4) The documents must be open to the inspection of any creditor or member of the company, without charge, and of any other person, on payment of such fee as may be prescribed (src:11833-11835)
GIVEN `the person is a creditor or member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee prescribed for any other person, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 859Q(4) terms of inspection`
`s 859Q(4) the terms on which the documents must be open to the inspection of the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is a creditor or member of the company`
    THEN `s 859Q(4)(a) open to inspection without charge`
    ELSE `s 859Q(4)(b) open to inspection on payment of the prescribed fee` `the fee prescribed for any other person, in pounds`

-- src:11836 | (5) If default is made for 14 days in complying with subsection (3) or an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused, an offence is committed by—
@ref s 859Q(5) If default is made for 14 days in complying with subsection (3) or an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused, an offence is committed (src:11836-11836)
GIVEN `the number of days for which default has been made in complying with subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
      `an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859Q(5) an offence is committed` MEANS
    IF `the number of days for which default has been made in complying with subsection (3)` AT LEAST 14 OR `an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made for 14 days in complying with subsection (3) or an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused, an offence is committed by—"

-- src:11837 | (a) the company, and
@ref s 859Q(5)(a) the company (src:11837-11837)
GIVEN `s 859Q(5) an offence is committed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859Q(5)(a) the company commits the offence` MEANS `s 859Q(5) an offence is committed`

-- src:11838 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 859Q(5)(b) every officer of the company who is in default (src:11838-11838)
GIVEN `s 859Q(5) an offence is committed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859Q(5)(b) the officer commits the offence` MEANS
    `s 859A both answers hold` (`s 859Q(5) an offence is committed`) (`s 859A both answers hold` `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` `s 1121 the officer is in default`)

-- src:11839 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 859Q(6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale (src:11839-11839)
`s 859Q(6) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE

-- src:11840 | (7) If an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused the court may by order compel an immediate inspection.
@ref s 859Q(7) If an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused the court may by order compel an immediate inspection (src:11840-11840)
GIVEN `an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859Q(7) the court may by order compel an immediate inspection` MEANS
    IF `an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused the court may by order compel an immediate inspection": the court's power is given for a refused inspection and the text does not say it has none otherwise

-- src:11841 | (8) Where the company and a person wishing to carry out an inspection under subsection (4) agree, the inspection may be carried out by electronic means.
@ref s 859Q(8) Where the company and a person wishing to carry out an inspection agree, the inspection may be carried out by electronic means (src:11841-11841)
GIVEN `the company and the person wishing to carry out an inspection under subsection (4) agree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859Q(8) the inspection may be carried out by electronic means` MEANS
    IF `the company and the person wishing to carry out an inspection under subsection (4) agree`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the company and a person wishing to carry out an inspection under subsection (4) agree"
